{{define "before"}}## Before you start

1. Sign in to Colliedesk and open **Settings → AI agents**.
2. Name the token (for example "{{.Host.Name}} on my laptop"), pick a tier (`draft` is a good start: the agent
   can sort and annotate, and nothing reaches a customer) and choose **Create token**. See [Agent tokens](sessions.md#agent-tokens).
3. Copy the token. It starts with `{{.TokenPrefix}}` and is shown once.

The steps below use `{{.Origin}}`: put the address you open Colliedesk at in its place.
Under **Connect your agent**, Settings shows these steps for {{.Host.Name}} with your address already in.
{{end}}

{{define "try"}}## Try it

Ask {{.Host.Name}}: "What can you do in Colliedesk?" It calls `colliedesk_whoami`, which answers
with your workspace, the token's tier and the tools it may use. Then, for example: "Triage the
open conversations nobody owns: tag billing questions with `billing` and leave a note with a
summary."
{{end}}

{{define "tiers"}}## What each tier can do

Colliedesk has {{.Tools}} tools. A token calls the tools of its tier directly; any other call
becomes an [agent request](agent-requests.md) a person approves in **Requests**.

| Tier | Tools it calls directly |
|---|---|
{{range .Tiers}}| `{{.Name}}` | {{.Callable}} of {{$.Tools}} |
{{end}}
Every tool and its tier: [Connect an AI agent (MCP)](mcp.md#tools).
{{end}}

{{define "revoke"}}Then revoke the token in **Settings → Sessions**: it stops working at once, wherever it was
copied.
{{end}}

